From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode-port <port@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 03:01:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] D515 code mode: a function body's declarations do not hide
 tools from its parameter defaults

Upstream: scanTools gives a function one scope for its parameters and its body's declarations, but parameter
default expressions are evaluated before the body's scope exists. `const f = function (a = tools.danger({})) {
var tools }; await f()` scans as no tools (also with `let tools` in an arrow body), though the default calls the
real tools. As with D514, code mode then fails the call as an unknown tool and a schedule check under-reports.
Fixed: the parameters are the function's scope, and its body block adds the body's declarations (var included).
Found by the Rust opencode-codemode crate.
Scenarios: codemode-tools.test.ts "codemode tool scan scopes" (new)
Upstream tests: packages/codemode/test/scan.test.ts adds a test

